\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VIII}{\ignorespaces Encoder equivariance class behind the \emph  {identical} invariant cut and pooling (isolating the steerable machinery): a lighter $E(n)$ (EGNN) encoder against the steerable $e3nn$ encoder and the hand-crafted invariants. Mean over $3$ seeds $\times $ $5$ folds; hash-locked inputs; no retraining. All three are exactly viewpoint-invariant --- a theorem for EGRU/InvariantGRU, and an fp32 certificate of $1.4\times 10^{-5}$ for EGNN\,$+$\,cut. ``Node-fail'' is MAD lost over $8$ dead joints. Damping the EGNN coordinate updates (clamp $0.1/0.5/1.0$) gives $+6.42/+6.06/+5.69$ --- the gap does not close.}}{14}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
